  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent heavy rainfall in South Jakarta has led to secondary landslide activity, specifically impacting Jalan Langgar II in Pejaten Timur. This incident has disrupted local infrastructure and caused flooding across two residential areas, where water depths have reportedly reached 50 centimeters. The event follows earlier structural concerns in South Jakarta, including a notable landslide involving a padel court parking area in the Kemang district earlier in November, which raised questions regarding foundation construction. Indonesian disaster authorities have issued ongoing warnings for various regions across the archipelago, citing the potential for further flooding and landslides caused by heavy rain. Residents in vulnerable districts remain under advisory to exercise caution as seasonal weather patterns continue to influence geological instability in urban and surrounding areas.",
